The legal text is the Constitution of Nepal as published in English by the Nepal Law Commission
(www.lawcommission.gov.np, https://lawcommission.gov.np/content/13437/), a government body. The Commission's page
and PDF state no terms of use or reuse conditions. The words were not changed; they were only split into files and
lines. Credit for the bytes: Nepal Law Commission.

The Nepal Copyright Act 2059 (2002), section 4, lists matters that copyright does not cover, including court
judgments and administrative decisions. Legislation is not named there, so this repository does not rely on an
exemption: it relies on the text being an official publication, offered openly by the state for public reading. If
you need certainty for a particular use, ask the Law Commission.

The arrangement of this repository, its tables, commit messages and tools are by Lexifina and may be reused under
the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). This
repository is not legal advice and not an official publication.
